{
  "$comment": "VAPP-121 app EXPORT / IMPORT ×4: share an app as one JSON file. THE FILE = `<slug>` + `fileSuffix` (`working-hours.app.json`, `mime`), `{format, app: {name, icon, color, description}, package, records?}`: `format` = this fixture's `format`; `app` = the identity (icon / colour null when unset); `package` = the HEAD package as synced; `records` ONLY when the person switched `copy.includeRecords` on: every live record of the app as `{kind, data}`, oldest first (createdAt, then id), never ids, authors, times or GRANTS (a grant is the importing owner's choice: an import starts with none). `buildAppExport` is the pure reference every client replays (`exportCases`, compared as parsed JSON, key order free). EXPORT (`copy.export`) sits in the app row's … menu (web + desktop lists, phones' Apps list), the editor header's … menu and the app's settings page; it opens ONE dialog/sheet titled `copy.exportTitle` with a single Switch row `copy.includeRecords` (shown only when the app has records; off by default) and the `copy.export` button: web downloads the file, desktop saves it through the save panel, iOS opens the share sheet, Android the share intent (a FileProvider cache path). No app version yet = no Export. IMPORT (VAPP-176: New app has no dialog any more) = the Apps list band's `copy.import` pill (apps.json `copy.import`, before New app), opening ONE dialog/sheet = the import step titled `copy.importTitle`: a monospace multi-line field (`copy.importPlaceholder`) plus `copy.chooseFile` (the platform's file picker, `.json`); as the text changes (debounced) the client asks the SERVER (tRPC `apps.validateImport {teamId, text}`, the one authority ×4) and lists its `issues` inline under the field as `path: message` rows (destructive tone, monospace, at most `limits.issuesShown`, then `copy.moreIssues`); `copy.importAction` is enabled only with no issues and calls `apps.import {teamId, text}`, which creates the app (name/icon/colour/description from the file, the slug derived like New app) with the package as v1 noted `copy.importNote`, its records (each validated against its kind's schema, the team's record quota for all of them) as the importer's, and opens the editor. A BARE package (an object with `templates` and no `format`) imports too, named by its `name`. `parseAppImport` (TS, `importCases`) is the structural half the server runs before the package and record validators; its issue paths are JSON pointers into the file. Caps: `limits.importMaxBytes` per file, `limits.recordsMax` records per import, `limits.maxDepth` levels of nesting anywhere in the file (deeper = `/: is nested deeper than` the cap, before any validator walks it). A failed import = toast (feedback-states.json). CAPTURE (the `app-export` + `app-import` views ×5): Export opens on the seeded Working hours app with `copy.includeRecords` switched on; the import step holds `capture.importText` and lists exactly `capture.issues`.",
  "format": "exponential-app/1",
  "fileSuffix": ".app.json",
  "mime": "application/json",
  "limits": {
    "importMaxBytes": 4194304,
    "recordsMax": 2000,
    "maxDepth": 64,
    "issuesShown": 8
  },
  "copy": {
    "export": "Export",
    "exportTitle": "Export {name}",
    "includeRecords": "Include records",
    "import": "Import…",
    "importTitle": "Import an app",
    "importPlaceholder": "Paste an app file or a package",
    "chooseFile": "Choose file",
    "importAction": "Import",
    "importNote": "Imported",
    "moreIssues": "and {n} more"
  },
  "capture": {
    "importText": "{\"format\":\"exponential-app/1\",\"app\":{\"name\":\"Todos\"}}",
    "issues": [
      {
        "path": "/package",
        "message": "is required"
      }
    ]
  },
